              "kind": "markdown",
              "text": "It’s **JSON Lines**: each physical line is a separate JSON record. Read together in order, the records reconstruct the chat session; it isn’t one complete JSON object.\n\nThe file uses compact change records:\n\n- `{\"kind\":0,\"v\":{...}}` starts with session metadata, including the session ID and version.\n- `{\"kind\":1,\"k\":[...],\"v\":...}` records a value at a key path. For example, `k:[\"requests\",0,\"copilotCredits\"]` sets the credit usage for request 0.\n- `{\"kind\":2,\"k\":[...],\"v\":[...],\"i\":...}` records a request-list update; the request object contains the prompt, response, model, timestamps, and other details.\n\nFor usage, search for `copilotCredits`. Each value is for an individual request; add the values to estimate the session total. The transcript can also contain your prompts, responses, and context, so take care before sharing it."
